{
	"_about": "Round-by-round league stories for the news feed (scripts/core/LeagueStories.gd). Same shape as the career story's bank (data/tales/career.json): each angle declares the slots its phrases may use, and LeagueStories.validate rejects any other. Numbers come in ready-made from the slots (\"31 points\", \"six weeks\"), so a phrase can change the words around a number but never the number. Voice: a footy news desk, third person, plural verbs for clubs and nicknames (\"Fremantle were\", \"Dockers hold on\"). One phrase is picked per match and angle from a seeded hash, so a round always reads the same. No phrase may repeat the headline over your own result (Headlines.gd): never \"From N points down at\", \"We made that interesting\", \"Not much room to breathe\" or \"Nothing between them\".",
